514
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:07,000
Tannur... eh.
 
A tannour... yes.

515
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:09,000
Shajara kbire... shu hayy sh-shajara hayy?
 
A big tree... what is this tree?

516
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:10,000
Hayy tut.
 
This is a mulberry tree.

517
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:13,000
Tut... ma sha allah... ma sha allah.
 
Mulberry... mashallah... mashallah.

518
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:18,000
Hay tut... hayy difle... 'a l-yasar...
 
This is mulberry... this is oleander... on the left...

519
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:25,000
Mhm... l-bet ktir hilu... 'umuman shu anwa' il-ashjar il-hon
yani l-fawakeh, w th-thimar l-mawjude hon?
 
Hmm... the house is very beautiful... in general, what types
of trees are here, meaning fruits and the yields present
here?

520
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:27,000
Hon fi r-rumman 'anna...
 
We have pomegranates here...

521
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:29,000
fi burdgan... fi lemun...
 
there are oranges... there are lemons...

522
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:32,000
fi mishmish... fi 'aqqabiyat...
 
there are apricots... there are loquats...

523
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:36,000
w l-baqiye saru... snobar fi... fi snobar kaman.
 
and the rest is cypress... there are pine trees... there are
pine trees too.

524
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:39,000
Yani fina nqul innu mu'zam il-ashjar il-muthmire...
 
So we can say that most fruit-bearing trees...

525
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:43,000
Eh mawjude... bitsir... kil ashjar muthmire bitsir.
 
Yes, they are present... they grow... all fruit-bearing
trees grow here.

526
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:49,000
Il-mujtama' l-hon yani, ilu taba' madani willa faqat bi'i
fallahi 'ala ma huwe?
 
The community here, does it have a civil nature or is it
purely rural and peasant-like as it seems?

527
00:23:49,000 --> 00:23:51,000
Fallahi... fallahi kullna fallahin... yani.
 
Peasant... peasant, we are all peasants... you know.

528
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:55,000
Bi'tibar inku drastu fil-madine w rihtu 'al-madine w
ishtaghaltu kaza... ma ta'assartu?
 
Considering you studied in the city, went to the city, and
worked there... weren't you influenced by it?

529
00:23:55,000 --> 00:24:00,000
La ma min'tassar, nehna aradina hon w kil ahlna hon.
 
No, we don't get influenced, our lands are here and all our
family is here.

530
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:04,000
Yani bil-madine kan fi ma'ishe hnike, halla sar waqqafna min
l-madine w kil shi...
 
I mean, in the city, there was a livelihood there. Now we
have stopped everything in the city...

531
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:07,000
sar 3am niji 'a aradina w ben zeytun w...
 
we started coming to our lands, among the olive trees and...

532
00:24:07,000 --> 00:24:08,000
Rji'tu 'ala tabi'atkun...
 
You returned to your nature...

533
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:10,000
3a tabi'etna l-awwalaniye.
 
To our original nature.

534
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:13,000
Halla birki hon shayfa ktir hilwe... hayy shajaret saru mu
hek?
 
Now, the pool here looks very beautiful... this is a cypress
tree, right?

535
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:14,000
Saru... eh saru qadime...
 
Cypress... yes, an old cypress...

536
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:17,000
Bas khallina nukhtum hon... ma' hadretak...
 
Let's conclude here... with you...

537
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:19,000
shadd 'umra has-shajara hayy?
 
How old is this tree?

538
00:24:19,000 --> 00:24:21,000
60 sene...
 
60 years...

539
00:24:21,000 --> 00:24:22,000
60 sene...?
 
60 years...?

540
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:24,000
60 sene hayy...
 
This one is 60 years...

541
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:30,000
waqt lli abuy ija 'ammar hon, sar shajar zara' hon hadol...
 
when my father came and built here, he planted these trees
here...

542
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:37,000
sarwat w fi snobar kaman... kaman 'umrun kaman bil 50-60
sene s-snobarat...
 
cypresses, and there are pine trees too... the pines are
also about 50-60 years old...

543
00:24:37,000 --> 00:24:40,000
hon kaman tannur tani, w birke hilwe tanye...
 
here is another tannour, and another beautiful pool...

544
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:46,000
Ktir hilwe... ktir... hon tarras... zine w hek...
 
Very beautiful... very... there's a terrace here...
decoration and such...

545
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:49,000
Eh zine w hek...
 
Yes, decoration and such...

546
00:24:49,000 --> 00:24:51,000
Allah yu'tik il-'afiye... abu Aram shukran ilak...
 
May God give you health... Abu Aram, thank you...

547
00:24:51,000 --> 00:24:55,000
Allah y'afik... ahlan wa sahlan... ahlan wa sahlan ustaz
ahlan wa sahlan...
 
May God grant you health... welcome... welcome, sir,
welcome...

548
00:24:55,000 --> 00:25:15,000
[Muzîk]
 
[Music]

549
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:38,000
Ahlan bil-hajje... barke barra... shu l-qussa? Imshi juwwa.
 
Welcome, Hajja... you're sitting outside... what's going on?
Let's go inside.

550
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:39,000
Imshi juwwa.
 
Let's go inside.

551
00:25:39,000 --> 00:25:42,000
Barke 'am... qabl il-masa barke hon qiddam il-bet mabsuta w
mkayyfe...
 
You are sitting... sitting here in front of the house before
evening, happy and enjoying yourself...

552
00:25:42,000 --> 00:25:44,000
Ahlan wa sahlan... ei wallah.
 
Welcome... yes, indeed.

553
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:45,000
Jaw hilu...?
 
The weather is nice...?

554
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:46,000
Alhamdulillah.
 
Praise be to God.

555
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:47,000
Kull nahar btbriki bi-hal waqt hon?
 
Do you sit here at this time every day?

556
00:25:47,000 --> 00:25:49,000
Eh wallah... hon... hon...
 
Yes, indeed... here... here...

557
00:25:49,000 --> 00:25:50,000
Bintak hadretik?
 
Are you her daughter?

558
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:51,000
Bint ibni...
 
My son's daughter...

559
00:25:51,000 --> 00:25:52,000
Bint ibna...
 
Her son's daughter...

560
00:25:52,000 --> 00:25:54,000
Bint ibna... ya ahlan wa sahlan... hada betik ya hajje?
 
Her son's daughter... oh, welcome... is this your house,
Hajja?

561
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:55,000
Eh ahlan wa sahlan...
 
Yes, welcome...

562
00:25:55,000 --> 00:25:56,000
Fina ndkhul l-juwwa netfarraj 'aleh?
 
Can we go inside and take a look at it?

563
00:25:56,000 --> 00:25:58,000
Imshi sharref... imshi...
 
Come on, honor us... come on...

564
00:25:58,000 --> 00:26:01,000
Sharrefi... ahlan wa sahlan... sharrefi ukhti...
 
Please... welcome... please, sister...

565
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:05,000
Ana bhib dkhul 'a l-byut... shuf tabi'etha shlun...
 
I love entering houses... to see what their nature is
like...

566
00:26:05,000 --> 00:26:07,000
Ahlan wa sahlan...
 
Welcome...

567
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:10,000
Allah ysallmik... hada betik... shadd 'umru hal bet?
 
May God keep you safe... this is your house... how old is
this house?

568
00:26:10,000 --> 00:26:12,000
Wallah jama'... yani...
 
Well, quite a while... I mean...

569
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:13,000
Yani...
 
Meaning...

570
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:14,000
Fawq 70 sene hek...
 
Over 70 years, like that...

571
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:15,000
Fawq 70 sene...?
 
Over 70 years...?

572
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:16,000
Fawq 70 sene...
 
Over 70 years...

573
00:26:16,000 --> 00:26:18,000
Hon w hon... hon ish fi?
 
Here and here... what's in here?

574
00:26:18,000 --> 00:26:21,000
Lik hon ghrad... jihazi... bajjahhez...
 
Look, these are items... my trousseau... I am preparing...

575
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:23,000
Jihazik... fhimti? Rah ttjawwazi halla in sha allah?
 
Your trousseau... I see. You're getting married soon, God
