Huwa kaman halla 3am bijahhez... adawat kahraba'iye, w
ghurfet dyouf, w ghurfet nom w kil shi kaman...
 
He is also preparing now... electrical appliances, a guest
room, a bedroom, and everything as well...

599
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:49,000
Shu byishtighel?
 
What does he do for a living?

600
00:27:49,000 --> 00:27:50,000
Mwazzaf.
 
An employee.

601
00:27:50,000 --> 00:27:51,000
Hadretik?
 
And you?

602
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:53,000
Ana bil-bet, bas ana darsa idarat a'mal.
 
I am at home, but I studied business administration.

603
00:27:53,000 --> 00:27:55,000
Ya ahlan w sahlan fiki... khallina inshuf bet il-hajje.
 
Oh, welcome to you... let's see the Hajja's house.

604
00:27:55,000 --> 00:28:01,000
Sharrefi ya hajje... sharrefi...
 
Please, Hajja... please...

605
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:04,000
Betik ya hajje ktir hilu...
 
Your house, Hajja, is very beautiful...

606
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:06,000
w mbayyin... bet qadim...
 
and it looks... an old house...

607
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:08,000
Bet qadim...
 
An old house...

608
00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:09,000
Asari... hada hon ish shu hada?
 
Antique... what is this here?

609
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:14,000
Hayy tawla mshan il-madd... mshan is-sufra... sifra...
 
This is a table for spreading out... for the dining table...
the dining table...

610
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:16,000
Sharrefi...
 
Please...

611
00:28:16,000 --> 00:28:19,000
Helw ktir, as-salamu 'alaykum...
 
Very beautiful, peace be upon you...

612
00:28:19,000 --> 00:28:24,000
Halla hada... khallini ahki 'an heyde... shighl idik...?
 
Now this... let me talk about this one... is it handmade by
you?

613
00:28:24,000 --> 00:28:26,000
La l-banat... 3ammata.
 
No, the girls... her aunts.

614
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:28,000
3ammatak... yani banatik...
 
Your aunts... I mean, your daughters...

615
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:30,000
Leh... banati eh.
 
Yes... my daughters, yes.

616
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:34,000
Ktir hilwe... bturki trtahi...
 
Very beautiful... you sit and relax...

617
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:40,000
Betak ktir hilu... fi fi raahah nafsiyye, fi ruhaniyat hilwe
ktir.
 
Your house is very beautiful... there is psychological
comfort, there is a very nice spirituality.

618
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:42,000
Ahlan wa sahlan.
 
Welcome.

619
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:45,000
Alhamdulillah... hada bet qadim... bet jiddi.
 
Praise be to God... this is an old house... my grandfather's
house.

620
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:46,000
Bet jiddak?
 
Your grandfather's house?

621
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:47,000
Eh.
 
Yes.

622
00:28:47,000 --> 00:28:48,000
Qaddesh sarlo mtwaffi?
 
How long has it been since he passed away?

623
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:50,000
Shi 15-16 sene.
 
About 15-16 years.

624
00:28:50,000 --> 00:28:51,000
15-16 sene...
 
15-16 years...

625
00:28:51,000 --> 00:28:52,000
Eh.
 
Yes.

626
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:54,000
Hada illi bs-saqf shu hada... il-mhalliq bil-het?
 
What is this on the ceiling... hanging on the wall?

627
00:28:54,000 --> 00:29:00,000
Had barwaz... 3ammati 'amalu killu bil-id w l-hjar w
l-bahs...
 
This is a frame... my aunts made it entirely by hand with
stones and pebbles...

628
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:05,000
w bt-... taba' sh-sha'le... zabbatoh killu, lazzaqoh...
qasit...
 
and... of the torch... they fixed it all, glued it... shaped
it...

629
00:29:05,000 --> 00:29:06,000
Khalles yani...
 
Finished it, you mean...

630
00:29:06,000 --> 00:29:07,000
Eh.
 
Yes.

631
00:29:07,000 --> 00:29:10,000
Hada l-maktabe ish shu hay ya hajje, hay?
 
What is this library here, Hajja?

632
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:16,000
Maktabet xeyî mirşid... hecî... hecî.
 
The library of my brother Mirshid... Haji... Haji.

633
00:29:16,000 --> 00:29:21,000
Ew... pirtûkên dînî li camiya, gundan belav dikir. Wî
wextî...
 
He... used to distribute religious books in the mosque, to
the villages. At that time...

634
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:28,000
W aal am tqul... akthar min 3-4 marrat in'ad hadol... killo
wazza'u 'a l-jawame' w 'a l-jiran w 'a d-diya'...
 
And she says... more than 3 or 4 times these were
restocked... he distributed it all to the mosques,
neighbors, and villages...

635
00:29:28,000 --> 00:29:31,000
Ma sha allah... ma sha allah... Allah yarhamu...
 
Mashallah... mashallah... May God have mercy on him...

636
00:29:31,000 --> 00:29:32,000
Allah yarhamu...
 
May God have mercy on him...

637
00:29:32,000 --> 00:29:39,000
Hilu hes-sobya taba'kon... w hilu hek namat l-bina w il-
yani farshet l-bet...
 
Your heater here is nice... and the architectural style is
nice, and the way the house is furnished...

638
00:29:39,000 --> 00:29:42,000
Hada illi taht taht l-khizanet it-televizyon shu hada
l-abiyad...?
 
What is that white thing underneath the TV cabinet?

639
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:45,000
Hay sharshef hek... lme'... metel artim mo hek?
 
This is a sheet like this... shiny... like a cover, isn't
it?

640
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:47,000
Shighl id hada willa...?
 
Is this handmade or...?

641
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:48,000
La.
 
No.

642
00:29:48,000 --> 00:29:49,000
Intu shaghlinu b-id...?
 
Did you make it by hand...?

643
00:29:49,000 --> 00:29:55,000
La la... hada jahiz... bas nehne zabbatna w qassayna w
3amalna.
 
No no... this is ready-made... but we fixed it, cut it, and
worked on it.

644
00:29:55,000 --> 00:29:57,000
Ew perdeyên me ye, me bi xwe qes kirine.
 
That is our curtain, we cut it ourselves.

645
00:29:57,000 --> 00:29:58,000
Shu am tqul?
 
What is she saying?

646
00:29:58,000 --> 00:30:00,000
Am tqul... hiye prdaye minna bas nehne fassalnaha.
 
She is saying... it's a curtain of ours, but we tailored it.

647
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:04,000
Ana şitê xesilnaha we nezelnaha.
 
I washed the winter clothes and brought them down.

648
00:30:04,000 --> 00:30:05,000
Allah ya'tik al 'afiya ya heccî.
 
May God give you health, Hajji.

649
00:30:05,000 --> 00:30:07,000
Ktîr inbasatna b zîyartik.
 
We really enjoyed your visit.

650
00:30:07,000 --> 00:30:08,000
Ahlan wa sahlan.
 
Welcome.

651
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:10,000
W Allah yqawwîkî. Şebêbîkik ktîr hilwat,
 
May God give you strength. Your windows are very beautiful,

652
00:30:10,000 --> 00:30:12,000
Hadol qadîmat ktîr, hal bayt hada ktîr hilw hek.
 
These are very old, this house is very beautiful like this.

653
00:30:12,000 --> 00:30:14,000
Bîcîb hawa we tahwîye we şems hilwe ktîr.
 
It brings in air, ventilation, and very nice sunshine.

654
00:30:14,000 --> 00:30:18,000
Ê bi raba, agir dixe sobê, tijî roman e lê, rabe rabe!
 
Get up, put a fire in the stove, it's full of pomegranates
girl, get up get up!

655
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:23,000
Ana l-yom 'amîlilkum kibbe we labanîye, 'a ta'amuha la
şebab.
 
I made you kibbeh and labaniyeh today, to feed the guys.

656
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:24,000
Allah yarziqik.
 
May God bless you.

657
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Rabe bes, ji min ve rabe, rabe rabe!
 
Get up enough, get away from me, get up, get up!

658
00:30:26,000 --> 00:30:28,000
Bes rah ntawwil.
 
But we will take a while.

659
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:32,000
La la ma d'tawwilû, bes 'ama... wahid...
 
No no you won't take long, but just... one...

660
00:30:32,000 --> 00:30:34,000
Tayyib bes mindayyif min al-kibbe 'a serî'.
 
Okay, we will just try the kibbeh quickly.

661
00:30:34,000 --> 00:30:35,000
Ê ê.
 
Yes, yes.

662
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:36,000
Allah ya'tik al 'afiya.
 
May God give you health.

663
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:56,000
Ahlan wa sahlan.
 
Welcome.

664
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:07,000
Ad-day'a bi hal fatra min is-sine, bitkun xelîyet nahil...
 
The village during this time of the year, is a beehive...

665
00:31:07,000 --> 00:31:11,000
...li'anno mawsam iz-zeytûn, we mawsam ir-rumman.
 
...because it's the olive season, and the pomegranate
season.

666
00:31:11,000 --> 00:31:16,000
Mawsam ir-rumman intaha, walakin mawsam iz-zeytûn byimtadd
min awasit Tişrîn l-Awwal...
 
The pomegranate season has ended, but the olive season
extends from mid-October...

667
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:22,000
...la nihayet taqrîban Tişrîn ith-Thanî, we rubbama la
nihayet Kanûn l-Awwal kaman.
 
...to approximately the end of November, and possibly to the
end of December as well.

668
00:31:22,000 --> 00:31:31,000
Fa mu'zam rical al-qarya we nisa'a bikûnû fil aradî 'am
yiqitfû zeytûn bi hal fatra.
 
So most of the men and women of the village are in the
fields picking olives during this period.

669
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:35,000
Hallaq rah nrûh ma'kum bi hal faqra al-axîra,
 
Now we will go with you in this final segment,

670
00:31:35,000 --> 00:31:41,000
'ala basatîn iz-zeytûn we r-rumman mithlma nna şayfîn al-an
'ala yamînna.
 
to the olive and pomegranate orchards as we can see right
now on our right.

671
00:31:41,000 --> 00:31:48,000
Rumman al-laffan we aydan fî 'andhun rumman hamid we 'andhun
rumman faransî.
 
Laffan pomegranate, and they also have sour pomegranate and
French pomegranate.

672
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:53,000
Rah ninzil hon hallaq, nşûf hada
 
We will go down here now, to see someone

673
00:31:53,000 --> 00:31:55,000
min ahalî hal basatîn,
 
from the people of these orchards,

674
00:31:55,000 --> 00:32:10,000
nahkî ma'o 'an ar-rumman we az-zeytûn.
 
and talk to him about pomegranates and olives.

675
00:32:10,000 --> 00:32:12,000
As-salamu 'alaykum.
 
Peace be upon you.

676
00:32:12,000 --> 00:32:16,000
We 'alaykum as-salam we rahmetullah.
 
And peace and mercy of God be upon you.

677
00:32:16,000 --> 00:32:17,000
Allah ya'tîk al 'afiya.
 
May God give you health.

678
00:32:17,000 --> 00:32:18,000
Allah y'afîk, ya ahla we sahlan, al-hamdullah.
 
May God give you health, welcome, praise be to God.

679
00:32:18,000 --> 00:32:19,000
Nita'arraf 'alayk?
 
Can we get to know you?

680
00:32:19,000 --> 00:32:21,000
'Adnan Xelîl Murşid.
 
Adnan Khalil Murshid.

681
00:32:21,000 --> 00:32:22,000
Ya ahlan we sahlan fîk.
 
You are very welcome.

682
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:22,000
Abû eyş?
 
Welcome.

683
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:23,000
Abû eyş?
 
Abu what?

684
00:32:23,000 --> 00:32:23,000
Ahlan we sahlan b Abû Ronî.
 
Abu Roni.

685
00:32:23,000 --> 00:32:25,000
Ahlan we sahlan b Abû Ronî.
 
Welcome, Abu Roni.

686
00:32:25,000 --> 00:32:27,000
Hallaq nihna bi bustan rumman.
 
Now we are in a pomegranate orchard.

687
00:32:27,000 --> 00:32:27,000
We wadih inno r-rumman ya'nî maqtûq,
 
Yes.

688
00:32:27,000 --> 00:32:30,000
We wadih inno r-rumman ya'nî maqtûq,
 
And it's clear that the pomegranates are picked,

689
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:30,000
Ka'anno xilis al-mawsam?
 
done.

690
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:31,000
Ka'anno xilis al-mawsam?
 
As if the season is over?

691
00:32:31,000 --> 00:32:34,000
Xilis al-mawsam, ê tab'an min isbû'ayn taqrîban.
 
The season is over, yes of course, for about two weeks.

692
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:37,000
Şû qissat şuhrat Miskê bi r-rumman ya'nî?
 
What is the story behind Miske's fame for pomegranates?

693
00:32:37,000 --> 00:32:48,000
Ya'nî l-Miskê, rummanata xidme, xidmat ar-rumman. Iza
r-rumman ma xadamta, we ma saqayta, we ma bedda samad we
bedda...
 
Well Miske, its pomegranates are about care, pomegranate
care. If you don't care for the pomegranate, and you don't
water it, and it needs fertilizer and it needs...

694
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:52,000
rumman byikbar. Min ma kibir, bya'tî...
 
the pomegranate gets big. When it gets big, it gives...

695
00:32:52,000 --> 00:32:55,000
Mîzat rumman il-Miskê eyş huwwe? Kbîr?
 
What is the defining feature of Miske's pomegranate? It's
big?

696
00:32:55,000 --> 00:32:56,000
Kbîr, ê.
 
Big, yes.

697
00:32:56,000 --> 00:32:57,000
Ta'amto?
 
Its taste?

698
00:32:57,000 --> 00:32:58,000
Ta'amto tayyib.
 
Its taste is delicious.

699
00:32:58,000 --> 00:33:00,000
We meşhûr ya'nî.
 
And it's famous.

700
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:01,000
Meşhûr bi mentaqat 'Efrîn?
 
Famous in the Afrin region?

701
00:33:01,000 --> 00:33:03,000
Ê.
 
Yes.

702
00:33:03,000 --> 00:33:04,000
Xallîna nimşî hek şway.
 
Let's walk this way a little.

703
00:33:04,000 --> 00:33:09,000
Intû btizra'û r-rumman hon ya'nî la hatta tbi'ûh rumman
walla btizra'û rumman la hatta tsawwû minno dibs rumman?
 
Do you plant pomegranates here to sell them as pomegranates,
or do you plant them to make pomegranate molasses?

704
00:33:09,000 --> 00:33:15,000
Wallahî, ya'nî minşan dibs rumman wa wahid byistafîd minno
ya'nî.
 
By God, I mean it's for pomegranate molasses and one
benefits from it.

705
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:16,000
Ma btibî'ûh rumman 'adî?
 
Don't you sell it as regular pomegranates?

706
00:33:16,000 --> 00:33:17,000
Binbî'ûh.
 
We sell it.

707
00:33:17,000 --> 00:33:18,000
Bi-tbî'ûh rumman 'adî.
 
You sell it as regular pomegranates.

708
00:33:18,000 --> 00:33:19,000
Binbî'ûh lakan.
 
Of course we sell it.

709
00:33:19,000 --> 00:33:21,000
Şqad 'umr ar-rumman bi Miskê?
 
How old is pomegranate cultivation in Miske?

710
00:33:21,000 --> 00:33:24,000
Wallah taqrîban taqrîban ya'nî, beddak...
 
By God, approximately I mean, you would say...

711
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:26,000
...tihkî bil xamsa we 'işrîn tlatîn sine.
 
...you're talking about twenty-five, thirty years.

712
00:33:26,000 --> 00:33:27,000
Faqat?
 
Only?

713
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:28,000
Ê.
 
Yes.

714
00:33:28,000 --> 00:33:29,000
Qabla ma kan fî rumman?
 
There were no pomegranates before that?

715
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:30,000
Qabla zeytûn kan.
 
Before there was olive.

716
00:33:30,000 --> 00:33:31,000
Zeytûn.
 
Olive.

717
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:32,000
Kan qabla zeytûn.
 
Before it was olive.

718
00:33:32,000 --> 00:33:35,000
Hallaq ana ba'rif ya'nî min şî mîyat sine,
 
Now I know that about a hundred years ago,

719
00:33:35,000 --> 00:33:37,000
aktar şway hasab ma hakû lî,
 
a bit more according to what they told me,

720
00:33:37,000 --> 00:33:38,000
illî hakûna 'an tarîx id-day'a,
 
those who told us about the history of the village,

721
00:33:38,000 --> 00:33:42,000
qalû abal mîyye mîyye we tlatîn sine kan hon il-mentaqa
killa ahraş.
 
they said a hundred, a hundred and thirty years ago this
whole area was forests.

722
00:33:42,000 --> 00:33:46,000
Ya'nî sarw we sindyan we ballût we hekî.
 
Meaning cypress, oak, and acorn and such.

723
00:33:46,000 --> 00:33:48,000
Ê...
 
Yes...

724
00:33:48,000 --> 00:33:51,000
ya'nî taqrîban bil mîyyat snîn, ê, tab'an ya'nî...
 
I mean roughly in hundreds of years, yes, of course...

725
00:33:51,000 --> 00:33:54,000
kan min hon la...
 
it was from here to...

726
00:33:54,000 --> 00:33:56,000
...Rîhanîye.
 
...Reyhanli.

727
00:33:56,000 --> 00:34:00,000
Kan ard ya'nî sahra mitl sahra, cbala...
 
It was land like a desert, mountains...

728
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:01,000
Zira'îye ya'nî.
 
Agricultural.

729
00:34:01,000 --> 00:34:03,000
Zira'îye, ahraş ya'nî, bûr.
 
Agricultural, forests I mean, wasteland.

730
00:34:03,000 --> 00:34:04,000
Bûr, ma ya'nî fadyî.
 
Wasteland, I mean empty.

731
00:34:04,000 --> 00:34:05,000
Ê mayy. Yitla' fîha aşcar hiracîye.
 
Yes, water. Forest trees used to grow in it.

732
00:34:05,000 --> 00:34:06,000
Aywa.
 
I see.

733
00:34:06,000 --> 00:34:08,000
Ba'den şeccarat.
 
Then they planted trees.

734
00:34:08,000 --> 00:34:13,000
Ba'den şeccarat, wal 'alam illî zara' zeytûn, illî zara'
rumman, illî zara'...
 
Then they planted trees, and people planted olives, planted
pomegranates, planted...

735
00:34:13,000 --> 00:34:14,000
...hinta we şa'îr.
 
...wheat and barley.

736
00:34:14,000 --> 00:34:18,000
Na'am. Sirr nacah ir-rumman hon inno fî 'andkum mayy wafra?
 
Yes. Is the secret to the success of pomegranates here that
you have abundant water?

737
00:34:18,000 --> 00:34:19,000
Ê, fî.
 
Yes, there is.

738
00:34:19,000 --> 00:34:22,000
Ir-rumman byinziqiy kam marra?
 
How many times is the pomegranate watered?

739
00:34:22,000 --> 00:34:26,000
Ya'nî taqrîban beddak aqalla şî aqalla şî arba' xams marrat
beddak tisqî.
 
Roughly, you need at least, at least four or five times to
water it.

740
00:34:26,000 --> 00:34:27,000
Faqat?
 
Only?

741
00:34:27,000 --> 00:34:28,000
Ê, ya'nî hada aqalla şî.
 
Yes, I mean this is the minimum.

742
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:30,000
Ya'nî kull ma saqayt ir-rumman,
 
I mean the more you water the pomegranate,

743
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:31,000
byikbar.
 
the bigger it gets.

744
00:34:31,000 --> 00:34:34,000
Ê mayy... mazot ğalî we l...
 
Yes water... diesel is expensive and the...

745
00:34:34,000 --> 00:34:38,000
...bta'rif ya'nî islahat il muharrikat ğalî, ê.
 
...you know repairing the engines is expensive, yes.

746
00:34:38,000 --> 00:34:41,000
Fî cadwa l-yom min zira'at ir-rumman?
 
Is there a benefit today from planting pomegranates?

747
00:34:41,000 --> 00:34:42,000
Şlon ya'nî?
 
How do you mean?

748
00:34:42,000 --> 00:34:45,000
Ya'nî l-fa'ida illî bit'ûd 'al-muzari' min zira'at ar-
rumman...
 
I mean the benefit that returns to the farmer from planting
pomegranates...

749
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:46,000
Ê.
 
Yes.

750
00:34:46,000 --> 00:34:46,000
Fî fa'ida kbîra?
 
Today.

751
00:34:46,000 --> 00:34:48,000
Fî fa'ida kbîra?
 
Is there a big benefit?

752
00:34:48,000 --> 00:34:48,000
Bil qiyas 'a z-zeytûn mathalan.
 
By God.

753
00:34:48,000 --> 00:34:50,000
Bil qiyas 'a z-zeytûn mathalan.
 
In comparison to olives for example.

754
00:34:50,000 --> 00:34:52,000
La', bin-nisbe laz-zeytûn, iz-zeytûn arbah min ir-rumman.
 
No, compared to olives, olives are more profitable than
pomegranates.

755
00:34:52,000 --> 00:34:53,000
Zeytûn arbah?
 
Olives are more profitable?

756
00:34:53,000 --> 00:34:54,000
Arbah.
 
More profitable.

757
00:34:54,000 --> 00:34:56,000
Li'anno z-zeytûn ma bedda isqaye.
 
Because olives don't need watering.

758
00:34:56,000 --> 00:34:57,000
Yisqû, 'andkum yisqû?
 
Do they water it, do they water it here?

759
00:34:57,000 --> 00:35:03,000
Ya'nî... marra martayn ya'nî... bes ir-rumman icbarî beddak
tisqîyo.
 
I mean... once or twice... but pomegranates you are forced
to water it.

760
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:04,000
Icbarî.
 
Mandatory.

761
00:35:04,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Icbarî, we iza ma saqayto ma byisîr.
 
Mandatory, and if you don't water it, it won't grow.

762
00:35:06,000 --> 00:35:11,000
Hallaq manzar ktîr badî', ktîr hilw ya'nî. R-rumman, hada şû
no'o hada r-rumman?
 
Now the view is very wonderful, very beautiful I mean.
Pomegranate, what kind is this pomegranate?

763
00:35:11,000 --> 00:35:13,000
Hada rumman laffan had.
 
This is Laffan pomegranate.

764
00:35:13,000 --> 00:35:14,000
Hada laffan.
 
This is Laffan.

765
00:35:14,000 --> 00:35:14,000
As-sinf illî mawcûd hon laffan aktar şî?
 
Laffan, yes.

766
00:35:14,000 --> 00:35:16,000
As-sinf illî mawcûd hon laffan aktar şî?
 
The variety present here is mostly Laffan?

767
00:35:16,000 --> 00:35:17,000
Aktar iş-şî l-laffan.
 
Mostly Laffan.

768
00:35:17,000 --> 00:35:21,000
Ya'nî l-fransî aqall, ya'nî qalîl byizra'ûh fransî.
 
I mean French is less, meaning few plant French.

769
00:35:21,000 --> 00:35:21,000
Ê.
 
Few.

770
00:35:21,000 --> 00:35:22,000
Ê.
 
Yes.

771
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:24,000
Fî şî byinziri' bi-zra'ûh bayn ir-rumman?
 
Is there anything they plant between the pomegranates?

772
00:35:24,000 --> 00:35:25,000
Ma fî şî, la'.
 
There is nothing, no.

773
00:35:25,000 --> 00:35:26,000
Abadan?
 
Never?

774
00:35:26,000 --> 00:35:27,000
La'.
 
No.

775
00:35:27,000 --> 00:35:28,000
We z-zeytûn?
 
And the olives?

